<p>Pro Forma Assumptions:</p>
<p>This unaudited pro forma financial information for the 10 quarters ended 7/26/97, based on management's good faith estimate of what operating performance would have been as a stand-alone corporation, is provided for comparative analytical purposes only.  Selling, general, and administrative expenses reflect a pro forma estimate of costs that HomeBase would have incurred related to corporate overhead activities performed by the Waban parent company.  These costs, estimated at $5.5 million in FYE 1/96 and $5.8 million in FYE 1/97 and FYE 1/98, have been allocated evenly between quarters.  Pro forma interest expense for all periods assumes that the capital structure that was put in place immediately after the BJ's distribution had been in place for all periods presented.  Components of interest expense are capital lease interest, mortgage interest, and credit agreement costs, all of which have been spread evenly, and bank borrowing interest expense, which has been spread to reflect the typical seasonal requirements of the business. The average estimated draw on the revolving credit facility is assumed to be $23 million. These unaudited financial data do not purport to represent the actual changes in the historical cash/borrowing position.  The provision for income taxes is estimated at 39.8%.  The number of shares used in the calculation of earnings per share is 37.9 million for all periods shown.  All pro forma adjustments are based upon available information and assumptions that management in good faith believes are reasonable under the circumstances.</p>
